      "content": "You'll want to focus on the predominantly Puerto Rican and African American crowds that were the backbone of the Bronx back then. Think rough-around-the-edges, hardworking individuals who've seen it all - the Puerto Rican extras can be dressed in their traditional 'boricua' attire, with a mix of American and Spanish flair, while the African American extras can be dressed in their signature 70s fashion, think afros, dashikis, and polyester suits. Don't forget to include some white working-class extras, likely of Irish or Italian descent, who make up the smaller but still significant portion of the population.",
